- **macnode**: the Mac is the hands node, reached from the VM with `mac-node <action> [args]` over an SSH session only the Mac opens, with no forwarding (the Mac runs `mac-node serve` as the hcron job `mac-node`; the VM side of the session is `mac-node bridge`, the forced command of the Mac's key). Actions, checked on both sides: `ping`, `eyes status`, `hands call <port-cmd> [args-json]` / `hands batch <json-array>` (armed for that request only; needs an unlocked screen), `chrome-mode <profile> [agent|desktop]`, `jobhunt <sub> [args]` (only the subcommands in the Mac's MACNODE_JOBHUNT_SUBS), `hcron status|list|pause|resume|run <id>`, `gh-code <company> [min]`, `portal-pass <id> [--create]`, `git pull <repo>`. Nothing else runs: no shell strings. Exit 75 = mac-offline: a non-GUI request is queued and runs when the link returns (`mac-node queue`, `mac-node result <id>`; `--no-queue` to skip); GUI actions (hands, portal-pass) are never queued, so ask again when the Mac is back. Exit 76 = locked: report it, never retry in a loop. 77 = refused, 74 = link lost mid-request (may have run; check before repeating). `mac-node status`, `mac-node log`. Secrets stay on the Mac: never ask it to print one. Setup: `__HARNESS_DIR__/modules/macnode/SETUP.md`.
